    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate (which is still rejected on a reused telephone) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and now carries `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate` is `false`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with getters/setters.\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)`, invoked only on create (after the hard-duplicate identity check). It finds an existing owner matching normalized lastName + postcode with a differing normalized telephone, picking the lowest id when several match, and sets the two fields accordingly (false / null when none).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the new fields; `possibleDuplicate` goes through a formatter that coerces null\u2192false so the response always carries an explicit boolean (mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`); `possibleDuplicateOf` maps by name.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` (the only test in the suite) passes.\n\nOne note: the acceptance base references a soft-delete convention (\"flagged deleted, so the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore it\"), but the current `Owner` entity has no deleted flag and no test exercises it here, so the new soft-match considers all existing owners \u2014 consistent with how the existing identity/capacity checks already behave.",
