        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns of this codebase:\n\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` lives in the service layer next to `countNamesakes` and `generateCustomerCode`, and is invoked from `saveOwner` under an `owner.isNew()` guard alongside the sibling create-time assignments (`setNamesakeCount`, `setCustomerCode`, etc.) \u2014 the natural home for this derive-once-at-creation logic.\n- Its implementation deliberately mirrors `countNamesakes`: same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()...filter(exclude self)` idiom and the same reuse of `Owner` static normalizers (`normalizeHousehold`, `normalizeTelephone`), matching how `generateCustomerCode` delegates to `Owner.customerCode`. A maintainer would find it immediately familiar, and there's no duplicated detection logic \u2014 it's the weaker-overlap counterpart to `assertIdentityIsUnique`, clearly documented as such.\n- The mapper's `formatPossibleDuplicate` follows the established `formatAgeBand`/`formatCheckDigit` convention (including the null-owner guard), and leaning on MapStruct's by-name mapping for `possibleDuplicateOf` avoids a redundant explicit mapping.\n- The model fields/accessors, the parallel schema edits across all four dialects, and the OpenAPI additions are all routine and consistent with the surrounding entries.\n\nNothing is in the wrong unit, nothing is becoming a catch-all, and no logic is duplicated."
